{"ranking": ["M4", "M7", "M3"], "fault": "Wrong gate connection on M4: its gate is tied to ibias instead of the mirror node a (the diode-connected M3 gate node), so M4 is driven fully on (Vsg ~0.97 V) and pulls node b to VDD into triode. That holds b high, keeps M7 off, and leaves the output inverter's input c low, so vout is stuck high. Reconnecting M4's gate to a should restore the mirror load, let b switch with the differential input, and fix polarity, tpd, and vout_min."}
